    "Condition : 1 - The proposal by reason of its size, design and position would not be subordinate to the existing house and would be detrimental to the appearance of the house and the street scene. The rear extensions would be overbearing, visually intrusive and would lead to a significant loss of light and privacy to the detriment of the amenities of adjoining occupiers. It is thereby contrary to Policies ENV.1.1 and H.3.4 of the Adopted Unitary Development Plan (1996) and Policies ENV-B.1.1, H.6.4 of the Proposed Alterations Revised Deposit Unitary Development Plan (2001) and Supplementary Planning Guidance on Revised Extensions Guidelines (2002)."
